1
00:00:01,502 --> 00:00:04,171
Hey! I got you a present!

2
00:00:04,212 --> 00:00:06,841
Oh, my goodness,
where did you hide it?

3
00:00:06,882 --> 00:00:09,259
I got it for your wedding
and I ordered it weeks ago

4
00:00:09,301 --> 00:00:10,719
and it finally got here.

5
00:00:10,761 --> 00:00:12,387
You didn't have
to get us anything.

6
00:00:12,429 --> 00:00:13,639
You already did so...

7
00:00:13,681 --> 00:00:15,390
I love it! It's huge!
Let's open it!

8
00:00:15,432 --> 00:00:16,684
Open it!

9
00:00:19,102 --> 00:00:21,522
It's a Ms. Pac-Man machine!

10
00:00:21,563 --> 00:00:23,315
Oh, my God!

11
00:00:23,357 --> 00:00:24,483
I didn't know
where to put it

12
00:00:24,525 --> 00:00:25,943
so I left it
here for now.

13
00:00:25,985 --> 00:00:27,736
Maybe we can put it
in the guest bedroom.

14
00:00:27,778 --> 00:00:29,446
Yeah, okay.

15
00:00:33,492 --> 00:00:35,160
I kind of like it here.

16
00:00:35,202 --> 00:00:36,578
So do you really like it?

17
00:00:36,620 --> 00:00:38,121
Are you kidding?
I practically spent

18
00:00:38,163 --> 00:00:39,832
my entire childhood
at the arcade.

19
00:00:39,874 --> 00:00:41,166
This is like...
oh, my God.

20
00:00:41,208 --> 00:00:42,668
This is like
my second-favorite game.

21
00:00:42,710 --> 00:00:44,252
Oh, really,
what was your first?

22
00:00:44,294 --> 00:00:45,713
Well, I don't really remember
the name of it.

23
00:00:45,754 --> 00:00:48,423
Well, what'd it do?

24
00:00:48,465 --> 00:00:50,759
Well, just... you put
a quarter in and, you know

25
00:00:50,801 --> 00:00:53,387
pull some handles and you win
like, a candy bar or something.

26
00:00:53,428 --> 00:00:54,805
A vending machine?

27
00:00:54,847 --> 00:00:56,891
Hey, don't feel bad for me.

28
00:00:56,932 --> 00:00:58,642
I won every time.

29
00:01:05,524 --> 00:01:10,404
♪ So no one told you
life was gonna be this way ♪

30
00:01:10,445 --> 00:01:12,865
♪ Your job's a joke,
you're broke ♪

31
00:01:12,907 --> 00:01:15,116
♪ Your love life's D.O.A. ♪

32
00:01:15,158 --> 00:01:19,955
♪ It's like you're always
stuck in second gear ♪

33
00:01:19,997 --> 00:01:22,290
♪ When it hasn't been
your day, your week ♪

34
00:01:22,332 --> 00:01:25,544
♪ Your month,
or even your year ♪

35
00:01:25,586 --> 00:01:28,797
♪ But I'll be there for you ♪

36
00:01:28,839 --> 00:01:34,845
♪ 'Cause you're there
for me, too. ♪

37
00:01:38,390 --> 00:01:39,433
Hey.

38
00:01:39,474 --> 00:01:40,893
I'm so glad you
guys are here.

39
00:01:40,935 --> 00:01:42,394
I've been dying to tell someone
what happened

40
00:01:42,436 --> 00:01:44,646
in the Paleontology department
today.

41
00:01:44,688 --> 00:01:48,650
You think he saw us or
can we still slip out?

42
00:01:48,692 --> 00:01:53,030
Professor Newman, the head of
the department is retiring so...

43
00:01:53,072 --> 00:01:54,698
They made you head
of the department.

44
00:01:54,740 --> 00:01:59,202
No, I get to teach
one of his advanced classes.

45
00:01:59,244 --> 00:02:01,329
Why didn't I get
head of the department?

46
00:02:03,040 --> 00:02:06,543
Oh, hey, Rach, listen,
I got a big date coming up.

47
00:02:06,585 --> 00:02:08,045
Do you know of
a good restaurant?

48
00:02:08,087 --> 00:02:10,005
Uh, Paul's Cafe.

49
00:02:10,047 --> 00:02:13,341
It's got great food and
it's really romantic.

50
00:02:13,383 --> 00:02:14,885
Ooh, great, thanks.

51
00:02:14,927 --> 00:02:16,887
Ooh, and then afterwards
you could take her

52
00:02:16,929 --> 00:02:18,597
